# Credentials for the MCP server. Copy to mcp-server/.env and fill in.
# Not committed — .gitignore covers .env at any depth.

SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co

# The scoped role's key, created by task 1.4 (migration 0028_mcp_role.sql).
# NOT the service-role key: that bypasses row-level security entirely, and the
# point of this server is to hand the model a door rather than the building.
CONTENT_MCP_KEY=

# Optional. How long to wait on the database before giving up. Default 15000.
# CONTENT_MCP_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# ── Refreshing the reference writers. Both optional, and NOT interchangeable ──
#
# scripts/scrape-sentinels.mjs fetches the eight writers' recent posts. Without either key, what is
# already stored stays readable and simply stops being refreshed. `refresh_sentinels` re-measures
# the stored posts and needs neither.
#
# 1) The Thought Pilot scraping console. Fast — 44s for a profile, measured — and already paid for.
#    It is OUR infrastructure, so a system that can only refresh this way depends on us, which is
#    the one thing clause 14.3 says must not be true of anything here.
#
#    It also returns post text with the line breaks STRIPPED. Verified 9 October: 70 of 70 posts
#    came back as one unbroken paragraph. Every shape measurement — paragraphs, words above the
#    fold, how a post opens and closes, list use — is counted from line breaks, so this backend can
#    answer "what have they written lately" and cannot answer "has their structure moved".
# XP_API_KEY=xp_live_...
# XP_BASE=https://scraping.thought-pilot.co/api
#
# 2) Apify, which Josh named himself at the kickoff call. Slower and charged per run, but the text
#    keeps its line breaks, so it is the only backend that can feed a shape refresh — and it is a
#    vendor rather than a single self-hosted service, which is why it stays wired in.
#
#    A token is one page in the Apify console, under Settings -> Integrations.
# APIFY_TOKEN=apify_api_...
